          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<h3 id=\"key-learning-takeaways\">\ud83d\udca1 Key Learning Takeaways</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Polynomial Expansion &amp; Overfitting:</strong> Increasing the degree allows the model to capture non-linear patterns, but high degrees without regularization lead to severe <strong>overfitting</strong> (extreme wild curves and giant weight values).</li>\n<li><strong>L2 Regularization (Ridge):</strong> Shrinks feature weights toward zero smoothly, reducing variance without driving coefficients completely to zero.</li>\n<li><strong>L1 Regularization (Lasso):</strong> Forces redundant or insignificant feature weights strictly to <strong>0</strong>, performing implicit feature selection.</li>\n<li><strong>Outlier Sensitivity:</strong> Linear models fitted with Mean Squared Error (MSE) or standard Log Loss can be heavily skewed by high-leverage outliers.</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
